{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/370363-multiple-covers-and-merits-at-character-creation","id":370363,"title":"Multiple Covers and Merits at Character Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-14T17:21:30-08:00","id":370363,"title":"Multiple Covers and Merits at Character Creation","content":"I was looking through the ready-made character pack and noticed that Ivy's default character technically has eleven merit dots. Ivy's Contacts (Hacktivists) - 1 switches to Contacts (Homeless) 1 in her second cover.<br /> <br /> Should the assumption be, if you're creating a character with multiple covers should a merit dot applied to one cover apply to both? I guess you can make an argument for and maybe draw some some support for it from the &quot;Lambet as a Cover&quot; sidebar in the core book but this wouldn't have been my initial interpretation.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T18:49:24-08:00","id":370562,"title":"","content":"I've always been in favor of the notion that different Covers can configure their Merit dots differently. I\u2019m glad to see some support for this notion, even if only in the form of different Contacts for different Covers. That said, it opens the door to some messy questions, such as whether or not one Cover can have more Merit dots than another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T11:00:38-08:00","id":371239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/370363-multiple-covers-and-merits-at-character-creation?p=370562#post370562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always been in favor of the notion that different Covers can configure their Merit dots differently. I\u2019m glad to see some support for this notion, even if only in the form of different Contacts for different Covers. That said, it opens the door to some messy questions, such as whether or not one Cover can have more Merit dots than another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see why they couldn't... Benny the Boring Plumber probably should not have access to Marty McNinja's Fighting styles, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T12:03:43-08:00","id":371285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/370363-multiple-covers-and-merits-at-character-creation?p=371239#post371239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't see why they couldn't... Benny the Boring Plumber probably should not have access to Marty McNinja's Fighting styles, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also don't see why they couldn't, but I wouldn't use Fighting Merits as the reasoning why. There's a section in the corebook (pp. 118-119) where it talks about Merits associated with Cover identities versus Merits associated with the demon alone \u2014 basically, physical features and social connections are Cover-associated, while knowledge and skills are universally available. Most of the Fighting Merits strike me less as physically built up and more as having trained and learned the right techniques and reflexes to use.<br /> <br /> If Benny the Plumber and Marty McNinja are secretly the same person, then Benny should have access to Marty's fighting skills. That doesn't mean it's a smart move for Benny to bust them out \u2014 that could mean a compromise to threaten Cover and attract enemy attention. Same principle behind the extra fourth specialty demons get; demons have an ongoing tension where they have abilities that are convenient to use, but often dangerous to let on.<br /> <br /> As for the OP, I tend to run with the demon having to distribute a single character's worth of Merits among all the demon's Covers, where Cover-specific Merits are concerned, rather than having social Merits and the like do double duty. Seems more like a point of personal preference than something that would break the game, though; an extra dot of Contacts isn't going to distort gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T15:05:51-08:00","id":371481,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}